It is not advisable to discharge industrial wastewater into rivers without proper treatment, as this could have serious environmental and legal consequences. You should look into more sustainable options such as investing in adequate wastewater treatment systems to ensure that the water released meets government regulations before being discharged. Additionally, you may want to explore alternative methods of waste management or consider using greener processes that produce less pollution in the first place.user

Using green technologies and processes is a great way to reduce your factory's environmental impact while still meeting regulatory requirements. Investing in water treatment systems that use natural biological processes or membrane filtration can help you effectively remove pollutants from industrial wastewater before it is released, making it a more environmentally friendly option than simply discharging untreated waste into rivers. Additionally, implementing measures such as source reduction and energy-efficient equipment may further reduce the amount of pollution generated by your factory, allowing you to meet regulatory standards more easily.assistant

